குறு","tr":"makaḷkuṟu","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"மகள்","tr":"makaḷ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"குறு","tr":"kuṟu"}]},{"text":"கினல்லது","tr":"kiṉallatu","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"கினல்","tr":"kiṉal"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"லது","tr":"latu"}]}],[{"text":"பீடுகெ","tr":"pīṭuke","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"பீ","tr":"pī"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"டுகெ","tr":"ṭuke"}]},{"text":"ழுமன்னர்","tr":"ḻumaṉṉar","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"ழுமன்","tr":"ḻumaṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"னர்","tr":"ṉar"}]},{"text":"குறுகலோ","tr":"kuṟukalō","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குறு","tr":"kuṟu"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"கலோ","tr":"kalō"}]},{"text":"வரிதே","tr":"varitē","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"வரி","tr":"vari"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தே","tr":"tē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"மன்ற","parts":[{"text":"மன்ற","lemma":"மன்ற","gloss":"of the common ground"}],"gloss":"of the common ground","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பலவின்","parts":[{"text":"பலவு","lemma":"palavu","gloss":"jackfruit tree"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"genitive suffix"}],"gloss":"of the jackfruit tree"},{"surface":"மாச்சினை","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"mā","gloss":"dark/large"},{"text":"சினை","lemma":"ciṉai","gloss":"branch"}],"gloss":"dark branch"},{"surface":"மந்தி","parts":[{"text":"மந்தி","lemma":"manti","gloss":"female monkey"}],"gloss":"female monkey"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இரவலர்","parts":[{"text":"இரவலர்","lemma":"iravalar","gloss":"suppliants"}],"gloss":"suppliants"},{"surface":"நாற்றிய","parts":[{"text":"நாற்று","lemma":"nāṟṟu","gloss":"to hang"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"hung"},{"surface":"விசிகூடு","parts":[{"text":"விசி","lemma":"vici","gloss":"tight binding"},{"text":"கூடு","lemma":"kūṭu","gloss":"frame"}],"gloss":"tightly bound frame"},{"surface":"முழவின்","parts":[{"text":"முழவு","lemma":"muḻavu","gloss":"drum"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"genitive suffix"}],"gloss":"of the drum"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடின்","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"sweet"}],"gloss":"sweet-sounding"},{"surface":"தெண்கண்","parts":[{"text":"தெண்கண்","lemma":"தெண்கண்","gloss":"clear drumhead"}],"gloss":"clear drumhead","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கனி","parts":[{"text":"கனி","lemma":"kaṉi","gloss":"fruit"}],"gloss":"fruit"},{"surface":"செத்து","parts":[{"text":"செத்து","lemma":"cettu","gloss":"mistaking"}],"gloss":"mistaking"},{"surface":"அடிப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"அடி","lemma":"aṭi","gloss":"to beat"},{"text":"பின்","lemma":"piṉ","gloss":"conditional suffix"}],"gloss":"if she taps"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அன்னச்","parts":[{"text":"அன்னச்","lemma":"அன்னச்","gloss":"swan"}],"gloss":"swan","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சேவல்","parts":[{"text":"சேவல்","lemma":"cēval","gloss":"male bird"}],"gloss":"male swan"},{"surface":"மாறு","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"māṟu","gloss":"in response"}],"gloss":"in response"},{"surface":"எழுந்து","parts":[{"text":"எழு","lemma":"eḻu","gloss":"to rise"},{"text":"உந்து","lemma":"untu","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"rising"},{"surface":"ஆலும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"āl","gloss":"to dance"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"habitual future suffix"}],"gloss":"dances"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கழல்","parts":[{"text":"கழல்","lemma":"kaḻal","gloss":"heroic anklet"}],"gloss":"heroic anklet"},{"surface":"தொடி","parts":[{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"toṭi","gloss":"armlet"}],"gloss":"armlet"},{"surface":"ஆஅய்","parts":[{"text":"ஆஅய்","lemma":"ஆஅய்","gloss":"King Ay"}],"gloss":"King Ay","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மழை","parts":[{"text":"மழை","lemma":"maḻai","gloss":"cloud"}],"gloss":"cloud"},{"surface":"தவழ்","parts":[{"text":"தவழ்","lemma":"tavaḻ","gloss":"to crawl"}],"gloss":"crawling"},{"surface":"பொதியில்","parts":[{"text":"பொதியில்","lemma":"potiyil","gloss":"Mount Podiyil"}],"gloss":"Mount Podiyil"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"to dance"}],"gloss":"dancing"},{"surface":"மகள்","parts":[{"text":"மகள்","lemma":"makaḷ","gloss":"woman"}],"gloss":"woman"},{"surface":"குறுகின்","parts":[{"text":"குறுகு","lemma":"kuṟuku","gloss":"to approach"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"conditional suffix"}],"gloss":"if she approaches"},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"it"}],"gloss":"except"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பீடுகெழு","parts":[{"text":"பீடு","lemma":"pīṭu","gloss":"pride"},{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"glorious"},{"surface":"மன்னர்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னர்","lemma":"maṉṉar","gloss":"kings"}],"gloss":"kings"},{"surface":"குறுகலோ","parts":[{"text":"குறுகல்","lemma":"kuṟukal","gloss":"approaching"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"approaching indeed"},{"surface":"அரிதே","parts":[{"text":"அரிது","lemma":"aritu","gloss":"rare"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is rare indeed"}]}],"literal":"On the dark branch of the jackfruit tree in the common ground, a female monkey / mistaking the sweet-sounding clear drumhead of the tight-bound drum hung by bards / for a fruit, if she taps it, / a male swan rises in response and dances. / On the cloud-crawling Podiyil hill of Ay who wears heroic anklets and armlets, / except for a dancing girl who approaches, / for glorious kings, approaching is rare indeed.","translation":"On the dark branches of the jackfruit tree in the village common, bards have hung their tightly bound drums. Mistaking the sweet-sounding, clear drumhead for a ripe fruit, a female monkey taps on it. Hearing the sound, a male swan rises and dances in response. On such a cloud-crawling Mount Podiyil of Ay, who wears heroic anklets and armlets, none but a dancing girl can approach; for proud, warring kings, approaching it is impossible.","modern":"ஊர் மன்றத்தில் உள்ள பலா மரத்தின் கரிய கிளையில், இரவலர்கள் தொங்கவிட்டுள்ள வாரினால் கட்டப்பட்ட முழவின் இனிய ஓசையுடைய தெளிந்த கண்ணைப் பழம் என்று கருதி பெண் குரங்கு தட்டினால், அதற்கு மாறாக ஆண் அன்னப் பறவை எழுந்து ஆடும். வீரக்கழலும் தோள்வளையும் அணிந்த ஆய் மன்னனின் மேகங்கள் தவழும் பொதிய மலையை, ஆடும் கூத்த மகள் நெருங்க முடியுமே தவிர, பெருமை பொருந்திய பகை மன்னர்கள் நெருங்குவது மிகவும் அரிது.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Uṟaiyūr Ēṇiccēri Muṭamōciyār praises the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ by describing the unique nature of his mountain, Mount Podiyil. The poet depicts a peaceful scene where a female monkey taps on a bard's drum, mistaking it for a fruit, which prompts a male swan to dance. This image highlights how welcoming and safe the mountain is for artists, bards, and dancers who seek Ay's patronage. In contrast, the mountain is completely inaccessible to hostile, proud kings who come with military intent. Through this contrast, the poet beautifully illustrates Ay's dual nature of extreme generosity to the peaceful and absolute resistance to the aggressive.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,2.6],[2.6,2.7],[2.7,3.44],[3.44,4.0],[4.0,5.0],[5.0,5.4],[5.4,5.5],[5.5,5.8],[5.8,6.3],[6.3,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,7.5],[7.5,7.8],[7.8,8.3],[8.3,9.3],[9.3,9.6],[9.6,9.7],[9.7,10.3],[10.3,10.4],[10.4,10.8],[10.8,11.8],[11.8,12.1],[12.1,12.1],[12.1,12.6],[12.71,13.58],[13.8,14.29],[14.29,14.54],[14.7,15.0]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,1.8],[1.8,3.0],[3.0,3.1],[3.1,3.9],[3.9,4.5],[4.5,5.5],[5.5,5.9],[5.9,6.1],[6.1,6.4],[6.4,6.9],[6.9,7.9],[7.9,8.3],[8.3,8.4],[8.4,8.8],[8.8,9.2],[9.2,10.3],[10.3,10.6],[10.6,10.7],[10.7,11.3],[11.3,11.4],[11.4,11.9],[11.9,13.1],[13.1,13.4],[13.4,13.5],[13.5,14.0],[14.0,15.2],[15.2,15.6],[15.6,16.4],[16.6,16.8]]},"sync":[[["மன்ற","of the common ground"]],[["பலவின்","of the jackfruit tree"]],[["மாச்சினை","dark branch"]],[["மந்தி","female monkey"]],[["இரவலர்","suppliants"]],[["நாற்றிய","hung"]],[["விசிகூடு","tightly bound frame"]],[["முழவின்","of the drum"]],[["பாடின்","sweet-sounding"]],[["தெண்கண்","clear drumhead"]],[["கனி","fruit"]],[["செத்து","mistaking"]],[["அடிப்பின்","if she taps"]],[["அன்னச்","swan"]],[["சேவல்","male swan"]],[["மாறு","in response"]],[["எழுந்து","rising"]],[["ஆலும்","dances"]],[["கழல்","heroic anklet"]],[["தொடி","armlet"]],[["ஆஅய்","King Ay"]],[["மழை","cloud"]],[["தவழ்","crawling"]],[["பொதியில்","Mount Podiyil"]],[["ஆடு","dancing"]],[["மகள்","woman"]],[["குறுகின்","if she approaches"]],[["அல்லது","except"]],[["பீடுகெழு","glorious"]],[["மன்னர்","kings"]],[["குறுகலோ","approaching indeed"]],[["அரிதே","is rare indeed"]]]}